            <ArticleTitle>Introducing interventional pain services in a large african teaching hospital: challenges and opportunities.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>663-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/papr.12032</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is a need for interventional pain management in the developing world; however, there are many barriers to the introduction of interventional pain therapies. This brief report describes one approach to the introduction of interventional pain medicine to a Nigerian teaching hospital. Although many barriers exist, interventional pain medicine can be brought to the developing world, as demonstrated in this case series.</AbstractText>
